      "content": "ok i think i get the river thing. so basically the faster the cycle, the less the capacitor can actually block it. \n\ncould u give me a quick example of how this would look in a real circuit? like if i had a capacitor and i just kept cranking up the frequency on my signal generator, how would i actually see that reactance change in the measurements?",
